  <prompt>
    Add optional `widthPreference?: 'full' | 'half' | 'any'` field to `SectionMetadata`, default `'any'`. Set `widthPreference: 'full'` on the 6 entity-list widgets in `sectionMetadataCatalog.ts` (Communications, Documents, Invoices, Matters, Projects, Work Assignments) per owner clarification 2026-07-02.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE frontend framework developer. Extends `SectionMetadata` and updates catalog entries.
  </role>

  <goal>
    `SectionMetadata.widthPreference` field exists; 6 metadata entries set `'full'`; type test verifies field acceptance.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Communications, Invoices, Work Assignments have many columns (email subjects, invoice descriptions) and need full row width to display without truncation. Owner clarified 2026-07-02: all 6 entity-list widgets default to `'full'` (dense grids read best full-width; operator can override per-placement). Runtime dev-guard + wizard warnings come in task 015.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/types/</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/WorkspaceShell/sectionMetadataCatalog.ts</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">Framework schema stays in `@spaarke/ui-components`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-022">Shared-lib React-16-safe.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Owner clarification 2026-07-02: all 6 widgets default to `'full'`.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-dataset-grid-framework-r2/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-dataset-grid-framework-r2/spec.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-012-shared-components.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read spec.md § FR-04. Locate `SectionMetadata` type.</step>
    <step order="2">Add `readonly widthPreference?: 'full' | 'half' | 'any';` field with JSDoc: `Optional. Signals to the WorkspaceLayoutWizard whether this section renders best at 'full' row width, 'half' width, or is flexible ('any'). 'any' (default) — no wizard warnings. 'full' — wizard warns/blocks placement in multi-slot rows. 'half' — wizard warns on single-slot placement (too much whitespace).`</step>
    <step order="3">Update `sectionMetadataCatalog.ts`: add `widthPreference: 'full'` to 6 entries: `communications`, `documents`, `invoices`, `matters`, `projects`, `workAssignments`.</step>
    <step order="4">Type test: confirm `SectionMetadata` accepts the union type; existing catalog entries without the field still type-check (backward-compat).</step>
    <step order="5">`npm test` + `npm run build` — clean.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: → ✅.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Build + test</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/types/{SectionMetadata-location}.ts (modified)</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/WorkspaceShell/sectionMetadataCatalog.ts (modified — 6 entries)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`SectionMetadata` accepts the `widthPreference?: 'full' | 'half' | 'any'` field.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">6 entity-list metadata entries have `widthPreference: 'full'`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Catalog entries without the field type-check (backward-compat).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build + tests clean.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

